Q: Call a function when you finish typing A: <p><code>setTimeout()</code> returns a timer ID.  It is that timer ID that you must pass to <code>clearTimeout()</code> for it to work properly (you are passing the callback function to <code>clearTimeout()</code> and that is not how it works).</p>
<p>So, you need to store the return value from <code>setTimeout()</code> into a variable in a lasting scope that you can then later pass to <code>clearTimeout()</code> like this:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function changing() {
  alert('You stoped typing!');
}
var timer;

function change() {
  clearTimeout(timer);
  timer = setTimeout(changing, 2000);
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;input type="text" oninput="change();"/&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
